This is the third message. It mentions the word quokka exactly once.

It carries a longer body than the others, with several paragraphs, so that the
mailbox has messages of different sizes in it and the offsets the splitter records
are not all the same distance apart.

A mailbox with three messages in it is enough to catch a splitter that is off by
one at either end, which two messages would not.

